 march will begin into the  end of a very  painful time in our history but it is  just the beginning  an unprecedented effort is now underway  to manufacture  and ship tens of millions of doses in  the u.s  fedex and ups have been tasked with  delivering to every state  the precious cargo moves under guard of  u.s marshals  it's going to be hard to imagine this  going off without a hitch that there  likely are unanticipated issues that are  going to arise when you're shipping that  many vaccine doses all around the  country  the hope is that up to six different  vaccines will be available on a  widespread basis by late spring  enough for every american who wants it  by the end of the month of may or the  middle of the month of june  we would have produced enough vaccines  doses to  immunize the totality of the american  population  to get there the u.s will have to get  through the worst days of the pandemic  the cdc estimates two to three thousand  deaths per day  for the next two to three months models  suggest the u.s  is on track to record 500 000 deaths by  april first  what do people need to keep in mind over  the next few months  well that number one the vaccine is not  going to appreciably impact  our lived reality right now this is the  worst of it  and and so people really need to keep  their eye on the prize vigilance  practicing everything we've been talking  about  no travel absolutely none that means  that while an end is in sight it's not  here yet  but increasingly americans are willing  to accept a vaccine as a way forward  a poll released today suggests that 80  percent say they're willing to get  vaccinated  though half of that group says they  prefer to wait a little while longer  just to be sure it's safe donna  all right jackson prosco in washington  thanks it's official president-elect joe  biden will take office  in january today the 538 members of the  u.s  electoral college formally cast their  votes in what is a bit of a bewildering  process  president trump is still refusing to  concede but it's clear biden won  306 electoral college votes trump won  232  it takes 270 to win by law the meeting  of the electoral college must take place  today their ballots must arrive in  washington by december 23rd  and on january 6 the ballots will be  counted during a joint session of the  house and senate  joe biden will be inaugurated as the  46th president of the united states on  january 20th  and late today president donald trump  tweeted that u.s attorney general  william barr has resigned and will leave  the job just before christmas  barr has been one of trump's most  steadfast supporters  aetna erupts ahead of fiery night in  sicily  a dramatic rescue in australia after a  major storm whipped up  all this sea foam onto a popular beach  it engulfed a dog her owner ran into the  foam and  managed to find the dog and pluck her  out southeastern queensland and  northeastern new south wales are being  battered by heavy rainfall king tides  and  flash flooding and in italy mount  etna is at it again launching plumes of  ash and lava into the sky  mount aetna lit up the night sky over  sicily on sunday  it is europe's most active volcano some  ash did fall on nearby villages but  there's no risk to anyone's lives from  this latest eruption  a magnitude 2.7 earthquake was recorded  on the mountain before this and there  have been more than  a dozen aftershocks  next delivering hope without forgetting  we still have months to go  when 2020 started we had no idea what  we'd be wishing for almost 12 months  later  no idea how life would change and that a  virus would infect every country in the  world  now our collective wish is simple we  wish life would get back to normal  and today canada took the first steps  today the first real ray of light of  2020 appeared  a tiny vial a precious vaccine a promise  that one day  the pandemic will end i'm so grateful  to be the first personal support worker  to take this vaccine  we have been waiting for this for so  long the first vaccinations in canada  are injecting hope  into our winter of despair make no  mistake  there's a long road ahead of us but what  this represents  is hope finally the virus that has  infected every aspect of our lives  has been outsmarted public health  doctors have reason to rejoice  bc's dr bonnie henry even did a happy  dance  scientists collaborated to crack the  viruses code in record time  producing a safe and effective way to  inoculate us  against it putting kovid 19 on the  defensive  not us here we are in december  and we actually have a vaccine against  that new virus  being administered you know not even  within the space of a full year  to my mind that is unbelievable and it  is a remarkable achievement of science  but the agony is not over this image  captures it a calgary doctor on his  knees  head in his hands calling another family  to tell them the bad news  covet 19 is still killing canadians by  the hundreds  often they die alone or with a doctor or  nurse with them  the relief of the first vaccines is  tempered by the staggering losses of  those who had no way to fight the virus  today manitoba's chief nursing officer  read a letter sent  by a 13 year old boy imagine the  suffering  and terror knowing you or your loved  ones might not live  or play in the park or breathe without a  machine  think about the big picture and we will  get through this  together we are still facing a long cold  winter  it will be essential in the months ahead  to do all we can to limit the spread of  the virus  but today with these first vaccines at  least we know  healing is coming  and that is global national for this  monday i'm donna friesen  tonight's your canada is the sunset over  the crow's nest river near  lundbreck falls alberta there are  beautiful spots all over canada please  email us yours to viewers at  globalnational.com  thanks for watching hope to see you here  again tomorrow take care of yourselves  bye
 

